; This is a simplified Gerber file for the top copper layer of the gate trigger PCB.
; Coordinates in mm (scaled by 1000 for integers).
; D10: Trace width 0.8mm
; D11: Via or pad 1.0mm
; Traces: From LM393 pin1 to NE555 pin2, etc.
; Note: This is basic; use KiCad or Eagle for full Gerber export.
; To use: Save as circuit.GTL, zip with other layers for manufacturing.

; Example traces (approximate positions):
; 5V rail: X0Y0 to X50000Y0
; GND rail: X0Y30000 to X50000Y30000
; Gate IN to LM393: X0Y15000 to X10000Y15000
; LM393 out to 555: X15000Y15000 to X20000Y20000
; 555 out: X25000Y20000 to X50000Y20000

; Full Gerber would include all apertures and paths.
; For production, generate properly in PCB software.</content>
